WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.036 --> 00:00:23.468
Two months later, after the robbery at the bishop's home, a stranger entered a small French city at dusk.

2
00:00:23.469 --> 00:00:27.951
Carrying a knapsack and a walking stick, he looked like a laborer.

3
00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:32.225
Just as he arrived in the city, a fire broke out in the city hall.

4
00:00:32.226 --> 00:00:38.689
The man rushed into the building and risked his life to save two children—the police chief's children.

5
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:46.348
The stranger did not show his yellow identity card, and in the confusion surrounding the fire, no one asked him for it.

6
00:00:46.349 --> 00:00:53.745
And that is how Jean Valjean started a new life in a new city with a new name: Monsieur Madeleine.

7
00:00:53.746 --> 00:01:01.086
The city had once been famous for a special kind of black jewelry, but the jewelry industry had fallen on hard times.

8
00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:05.564
Madeleine, however, soon discovered a way to make the jewelry more cheaply.

9
00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:09.499
Everyone benefited from this new manufacturing process.

10
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:15.983
The factories made more money; the factory workers' wages went up, and consumers paid less.

11
00:01:15.984 --> 00:01:22.015
As for Madeleine, he built a large factory with separate workshops for men and women.

12
00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:26.800
He required that all his employees be honest and of good moral character.

13
00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:33.903
By 1820 he had made a fortune and deposited more than 600,000 francs in the bank.

14
00:01:33.904 --> 00:01:39.451
But before doing that, he spent more than a million francs on the city and its poor.

15
00:01:39.452 --> 00:01:47.808
He improved the hospital and replaced the miserable schoolhouse with two new schools, one for boys and one for girls.

16
00:01:47.809 --> 00:01:54.959
People begged him to become the mayor, but Madeleine refused, and nothing could persuade him to change his mind.

17
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.959
Then one day an old woman called out to him as he passed her doorstep.

18
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.038
"A good mayor is a good thing. Are you afraid of the good you can do?"

19
00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:12.935
Her words struck him, and soon he was Mayor Madeleine. Nevertheless he continued to live simply.

20
00:02:12.936 --> 00:02:18.443
He fulfilled his duties as mayor but led an isolated life beyond that.

21
00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:26.419
Although he was no longer young, he was still very strong and was always willing to lend a hand to anyone who needed help.

22
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:35.260
Whenever he went out, his pockets were full of money, but when he returned, they were empty because he had given it all away.

23
00:02:35.261 --> 00:02:40.769
The mayor was especially kind to chimney sweeps, who passed through the city looking for work.

24
00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.736
He always asked their names and handed them money.

25
00:02:43.737 --> 00:02:49.085
Mayor Madeleine was a pleasant man, but there was something sad about him.

26
00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:55.403
People saw him as a rich man who was not proud, a fortunate man who did not appear content.

27
00:02:55.404 --> 00:03:01.824
At the beginning of 1821, the local newspaper reported the death of Bishop Myriel.

28
00:03:01.825 --> 00:03:05.942
The next morning when the mayor went out, he was dressed all in black.

29
00:03:05.943 --> 00:03:09.649
Everyone wondered why he was mourning the death of the bishop.

30
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.054
"You must be a relative of the bishop's," one elderly woman said to him.

31
00:03:15.055 --> 00:03:18.211
"No, madame," he replied respectfully.

32
00:03:18.212 --> 00:03:21.387
"Then why do you wear mourning for him?"

33
00:03:21.388 --> 00:03:24.808
"In my youth I was a servant for his family."

34
00:03:24.809 --> 00:03:31.054
"Ah!" The woman seemed satisfied with his explanation and no one else questioned him.

35
00:03:31.055 --> 00:03:38.364
Time passed and everyone grew to respect the mayor. People came from thirty miles around to consult him.

36
00:03:38.365 --> 00:03:44.197
Mayor Madeleine settled differences, prevented lawsuits, and reconciled enemies.

37
00:03:44.198 --> 00:03:49.856
He seemed to have a sense of what was good and fair, a natural understanding of the law.

38
00:03:49.857 --> 00:03:56.927
There was, however, one man who held himself apart and refused to be drawn into admiring the mayor.

39
00:03:56.928 --> 00:04:01.674
His name was Javert, and he was an inspector in the police department.

40
00:04:01.675 --> 00:04:09.674
Often when the mayor passed along the street, acknowledging the greetings of his followers, Javert stood alone, watching him.

41
00:04:09.675 --> 00:04:15.761
"I know I've seen that man somewhere before," Javert said to himself. "But where?"

42
00:04:15.762 --> 00:04:23.341
Javert had been born in a prison. His mother was a fortune-teller and his father was a convict on a prison ship.

43
00:04:23.342 --> 00:04:27.272
In his youth Javert worked as a guard on a prison ship.

44
00:04:27.273 --> 00:04:33.904
He had great respect for authority, but he had nothing but disgust for anyone who broke the law.

45
00:04:33.905 --> 00:04:37.647
Harsh and judgmental, he made no exceptions.

46
00:04:37.648 --> 00:04:46.404
Javert would have arrested his own father for escaping from prison. Javert's role in life was to be a spy and an informer.

47
00:04:46.405 --> 00:04:52.642
Javert always kept an eye on Madeleine, an eye full of suspicion and speculation.

48
00:04:52.643 --> 00:04:58.285
The mayor endured this unpleasant and annoying stare without appearing to pay any attention to it.

49
00:04:58.286 --> 00:05:03.301
He treated Javert as he treated everyone else—with kindness and a friendly manner.

50
00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:10.888
One morning the mayor was walking along one of the back alleys when he heard shouting and saw a crowd gathering.

51
00:05:10.889 --> 00:05:14.373
A horse had been pulling a cart when it stumbled and fell.

52
00:05:14.374 --> 00:05:21.102
In trying to help the horse, its owner—an old man named Fauchelevent—had fallen under the cart.

53
00:05:21.103 --> 00:05:25.118
The cart was heavily loaded so there was no way to pull the man out.

54
00:05:25.119 --> 00:05:29.697
"Help!" cried Fauchelevent. "I'm being crushed to death!"

55
00:05:29.698 --> 00:05:38.094
Mayor Madeleine approached and the crowd parted. He quickly saw that the only way to free the old man was to lift the cart.

56
00:05:38.095 --> 00:05:40.720
"Does anybody have a jack?" he asked.

57
00:05:40.721 --> 00:05:44.269
"Someone has gone to fetch one," replied a peasant.

58
00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.067
"How soon will it be here?"

59
00:05:46.068 --> 00:05:50.999
"The jack is at the blacksmith's, but it will take at least a quarter of an hour to arrive."

60
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.737
"Fifteen minutes!" exclaimed the mayor as he watched the cart's wheels sinking in the mud. "We can't wait that long."

61
00:05:57.738 --> 00:06:01.983
"It can't be helped," said someone else in the crowd.

62
00:06:01.984 --> 00:06:08.412
"Listen," said Madeleine, "there's still room enough for a man to crawl under the wagon and lift it with his back.

63
00:06:08.413 --> 00:06:10.921
In half a minute, we'll have the poor man out.

64
00:06:10.922 --> 00:06:16.483
Is there no one who has the strength and courage to do it? I'll give him five gold coins."

65
00:06:16.484 --> 00:06:18.750
No one stirred in the crowd.

66
00:06:18.751 --> 00:06:21.172
"Ten gold coins!" said the mayor.

67
00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:23.491
The bystanders dropped their eyes.

68
00:06:23.492 --> 00:06:29.468
One of them muttered, "A man would have to be awfully strong, and even then he'd risk getting crushed."

69
00:06:29.469 --> 00:06:35.055
"Come, someone, anyone!" said Madeleine. "Twenty gold coins."

70
00:06:35.056 --> 00:06:37.033
The same silence.

71
00:06:37.034 --> 00:06:40.063
"It's not that they aren't willing," said a voice.

72
00:06:40.064 --> 00:06:44.127
The mayor spun around and saw Javert, who continued to speak.

73
00:06:44.128 --> 00:06:50.539
"But they don't have the strength. You'd need a terribly strong man to raise a cart like that on his back."

74
00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:56.293
Then Javert looked the mayor in the eye and said, "I've known only one man capable of doing that."

75
00:06:56.294 --> 00:06:57.872
Madeleine shuddered.

76
00:06:57.873 --> 00:07:04.769
"He was a convict on the prison ships at Toulon." Javert said this casually, but he never took his eyes off the mayor.

77
00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.879
Madeleine turned pale.

78
00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.198
Meanwhile the cart continued to sink in the mud.

79
00:07:10.199 --> 00:07:15.531
"I'm dying!" screamed Fauchelevent. "Will no one help me?"

80
00:07:15.532 --> 00:07:22.690
With Javert's eyes still on him, the mayor looked at the peasants who stood there watching, and smiled sadly.

81
00:07:22.691 --> 00:07:28.436
Then he fell on his knees and before the crowd could stop him, he was under the cart.

82
00:07:28.437 --> 00:07:33.356
There was an awful moment of silence as the mayor tried in vain to lift the cart.

83
00:07:33.357 --> 00:07:41.361
Then the victim himself called out a warning. "Stop!" cried Fauchelevent. "Or you will be crushed to death with me!"
